														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2007889">
									

<p>People getting worked up into killing each other over stupid shit is not a terribly anomalous or really even uncommon human behavior. I get that the anomalous part is the spooky/random sky octopus thing causing it, but on several levels this feels like a cheapening of real-life conflict. A lot of the article's supposed weirdness stems from the fact that this happening in First World locales and is encouraging violence against groups like &quot;people from Michigan&quot;, which I find kind of obnoxious (&quot;look, it's Americans killing each other over ethnic/ideological/religious conflicts, how wacky is that, guys?&quot;).</p>
<p>Aside from that, you've buried the shit out of your lede. We don't find out why exactly this is anomalous or what it even does until waaaay down into the article. Frankly, the only reason I finished it was because I had seen some of the earlier comments and knew what was coming. The octopus-in-the-sky stuff feels exceedingly random and tacked-on since you don't really go anywhere with it, which to me hurts the article's flow since I'm looking for why the hell that matters as I'm reading.</p>

							</div>

								
					
